{"content": "<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Why Is the Sky Blue? · 天空为什么是蓝色的？</title>
<style>
  :root{
    --bg:#fbfaf7;
    --panel:#ffffff;
    --ink:#1b1b1f;
    --muted:#71717a;
    --line:#e6e3dc;
    --l1:#d97706;
    --l2:#2563eb;
    --l3:#475569;
    --radius:14px;
    --sans:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",Roboto,"Helvetica Neue",Arial,
           "PingFang SC","Hiragino Sans GB","Microsoft YaHei",sans-serif;
    --math:"Times New Roman",Cambria,"Songti SC",Georgia,serif;
  }

  *{box-sizing:border-box}

  html{scroll-behavior:smooth}

  body{
    margin:0;
    background:var(--bg);
    color:var(--ink);
    font-family:var(--sans);
    -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;
    line-height:1.6;
  }

  /* ---------- progress bar ---------- */
  #progress{
    position:fixed;top:0;left:0;height:3px;width:0%;
    background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--l1),var(--l2),var(--l3));
    z-index:100;transition:width .08s linear;
  }

  /* ---------- nav dots ---------- */
  nav{
    position:fixed;right:22px;top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%);
    display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px;z-index:50;
  }
  nav a{
    width:9px;height:9px;border-radius:50%;
    background:var(--line);border:1px solid #d5d1c8;
    transition:all .25s ease;position:relative;
  }
  nav a:hover{background:#b9b4a9}
  nav a.active{background:var(--ink);border-color:var(--ink);transform:scale(1.25)}
  nav a span{
    position:absolute;right:20px;top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%);
    font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.09em;text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap;opacity:0;pointer-events:none;
    transition:opacity .2s ease;
  }
  nav a:hover span{opacity:1}

  /* ---------- layout ---------- */
  .wrap{max-width:1180px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 52px 120px}

  header.hero{
    padding:120px 0 64px;
    border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .hero .eyebrow{
    font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.22em;text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:26px;
  }
  .hero h1{
    font-size:clamp(2rem,4.6vw,3.3rem);
    line-height:1.08;margin:0 0 .28em;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.02em;
  }
  .hero h1 .zh-title{
    display:block;font-size:.62em;font-weight:500;color:#3f3f46;
    margin-top:.45em;letter-spacing:.02em;
  }
  .hero .sub{
    display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:40px;
    margin-top:38px;color:var(--muted);font-size:15px;max-width:900px;
  }
  .hero .sub .zh{line-height:1.9}

  /* ---------- slides ---------- */
  .slide{
    padding:76px 0 64px;
    border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);
    opacity:0;transform:translateY(22px);
    transition:opacity .7s ease,transform .7s ease;
  }
  .slide.in{opacity:1;transform:none}

  .kicker{
    display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;
    font-size:11.5px;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:30px;
  }
  .kicker .num{
    font-family:var(--math);font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.05em;
    color:#fff;background:var(--accent);border-radius:5px;
    padding:3px 9px;font-weight:700;
  }
  .kicker .rule{flex:1;height:1px;background:var(--line)}

  .cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:0}
  .col{padding:0 40px}
  .col:first-child{padding-left:0}
  .col:last-child{padding-right:0;border-left:1px solid var(--line)}

  .col h3{
    font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 22px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em;
    display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;
  }
  .col h3 .chip{
    font-size:10px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--accent);border:1px solid currentColor;border-radius:99px;
    padding:2px 9px;opacity:.85;
  }
  .col p{margin:0 0 18px;font-size:16px}
  .col p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
  .col .zh, .col p.zh{line-height:1.92}
  .col strong{font-weight:650}
  .col ul{margin:0 0 18px;padding-left:20px}
  .col li{margin-bottom:14px;font-size:16px}
  .col li:last-child{margin-bottom:0}

  #l1{--accent:var(--l1)}
  #l2{--accent:var(--l2)}
  #l3{--accent:var(--l3)}

  /* ---------- math ---------- */
  .eq{
    display:block;
    font-family:var(--math);
    font-size:1.18rem;
    text-align:center;
    margin:26px 0;
    padding:22px 16px;
    background:var(--panel);
    border:1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius:var(--radius);
    overflow-x:auto;
    line-height:1.5;
  }
  .m{font-family:var(--math);font-style:italic;font-size:1.04em;padding:0 1px}
  .frac{
    display:inline-flex;flex-direction:column;vertical-align:-0.55em;
    text-align:center;margin:0 .18em;font-style:italic;
  }
  .frac > span:first-child{border-bottom:1px solid currentColor;padding:0 .25em .06em}
  .frac > span:last-child{padding:.06em .25em 0}
  sup,sub{font-size:.68em;font-style:italic}

  /* ---------- closing ---------- */
  .closing{
    padding:80px 0 0;text-align:center;
  }
  .closing .rule{
    width:52px;height:2px;background:var(--ink);opacity:.18;
    margin:0 auto 40px;border-radius:2px;
  }
  .closing p{
    font-size:1.08rem;max-width:760px;margin:0 auto 18px;
    color:#2b2b31;font-style:italic;line-height:1.72;
  }
  .closing p.zh{font-style:normal;line-height:1.95;color:#3f3f46}

  footer{
    margin-top:64px;padding-top:28px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);
    display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;
    font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);letter-spacing:.04em;
  }

  /* ---------- responsive ---------- */
  @media (max-width:860px){
    .wrap{padding:0 24px 90px}
    nav{display:none}
    .hero{padding:84px 0 48px}
    .hero .sub{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:16px}
    .cols{grid-template-columns:1fr}
    .col{padding:0}
    .col:last-child{
      border-left:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);
      margin-top:32px;padding-top:32px;
    }
    .col h3 .chip{font-size:9.5px}
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){
    html{scroll-behavior:auto}
    .slide{opacity:1;transform:none;transition:none}
  }

  @media print{
    #progress,nav{display:none}
    body{background:#fff}
    .slide{opacity:1;transform:none;page-break-inside:avoid}
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div id="progress"></div>

<nav aria-label="Sections">
  <a href="#l1" aria-label="Level 1"><span>Level 1 · 第一层</span></a>
  <a href="#l2" aria-label="Level 2"><span>Level 2 · 第二层</span></a>
  <a href="#l3" aria-label="Level 3"><span>Level 3 · 第三层</span></a>
  <a href="#end" aria-label="Summary"><span>Summary · 总结</span></a>
</nav>

<div class="wrap">

  <header class="hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">A Bilingual Explainer · 双语科普</div>
    <h1>
      Why Is the Sky Blue?
      <span class="zh-title">天空为什么是蓝色的？</span>
    </h1>
    <div class="sub">
      <div>The same phenomenon explained three ways, from simplest to most rigorous.</div>
      <div class="zh">同一个现象，三种讲法，从最简单到最严谨。</div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- ================= LEVEL 1 ================= -->
  <section class="slide" id="l1">
    <div class="kicker">
      <span class="num">01</span>
      <span>Level One · 第一层</span>
      <span class="rule"></span>
    </div>

    <div class="cols">
      <div class="col" lang="en">
        <h3><span class="chip">EN</span>For a 3-Year-Old 🧸</h3>
        <p>The sun sends us light — and light is made of lots of colors mixed together! 🌈</p>
        <p>When sunlight travels down through the sky, it bumps into tiny bits of air. The little blue colors are bouncy and wiggly, so they bump and jump all over the place — bouncing everywhere across the sky!</p>
        <p>The red and yellow colors are sleepy and heavy. They go straight down to the ground where you are.</p>
        <p>So when you look up, you see all that bouncy blue light bouncing around up there. That's why the sky looks blue! 💙</p>
      </div>

      <div class="col" lang="zh-Hans">
        <h3><span class="chip">中文</span>讲给三岁小朋友 🧸</h3>
        <p class="zh">太阳把光照到我们这里——而光啊，是好多好多颜色混在一起的！🌈</p>
        <p class="zh">阳光穿过天空往下走的时候，会撞到空气里的小小颗粒。蓝色这些小颜色又蹦又跳、特别活泼，一撞就到处乱弹——在整个天空中蹦来蹦去！</p>
        <p class="zh">红色和黄色呢，它们又困又重，就直直地落到地上，落到你身边。</p>
        <p class="zh">所以你抬头看的时候，看到的就是那些在头顶上蹦蹦跳跳的蓝光。这就是天空看起来是蓝色的原因啦！💙</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= LEVEL 2 ================= -->
  <section class="slide" id="l2">
    <div class="kicker">
      <span class="num">02</span>
      <span>Level Two · 第二层</span>
      <span class="rule"></span>
    </div>

    <div class="cols">
      <div class="col" lang="en">
        <h3><span class="chip">EN</span>For a High School Teenager 🎒</h3>
        <p>Sunlight looks white, but it's really a mix of all visible wavelengths — from red (~700&nbsp;nm) to violet (~400&nbsp;nm). When it enters the atmosphere, it collides with nitrogen and oxygen molecules that are much smaller than the light's wavelength.</p>
        <p>This causes <strong>Rayleigh scattering</strong>, where light is scattered by particles smaller than its wavelength. The key detail: the amount of scattering is inversely proportional to the <strong>fourth power of the wavelength</strong>:</p>
        <div class="eq"><span class="m">I</span> ∝ <span class="frac"><span>1</span><span><span class="m">λ</span><sup>4</sup></span></span></div>
        <p>So blue light (~450&nbsp;nm) scatters roughly <strong>6–7 times more</strong> than red light (~700&nbsp;nm). That scattered blue light gets redirected in every direction across the sky, so no matter where you look, blue light is reaching your eyes from all over.</p>
        <p>Two natural follow-up questions:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Why not violet?</strong> Violet scatters even more than blue — but the Sun emits less violet, our eyes are less sensitive to it, and some of it gets absorbed in the upper atmosphere. The mix averages out to the blue we perceive.</li>
          <li><strong>Why are sunsets red?</strong> At sunset, sunlight travels through much more atmosphere. The blue gets scattered away <em>before</em> it reaches you, leaving the long-wavelength reds and oranges to come straight through.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="col" lang="zh-Hans">
        <h3><span class="chip">中文</span>讲给高中生 🎒</h3>
        <p class="zh">阳光看起来是白色的，但它其实是所有可见波长的混合——从红光（约 700 nm）到紫光（约 400 nm）。当阳光进入大气层，会撞上氮气和氧气分子，而这些分子比光的波长小得多。</p>
        <p class="zh">这就产生了<strong>瑞利散射</strong>：光被比其波长更小的颗粒散射。关键的一点是，散射的强度与<strong>波长的四次方</strong>成反比：</p>
        <div class="eq"><span class="m">I</span> ∝ <span class="frac"><span>1</span><span><span class="m">λ</span><sup>4</sup></span></span></div>
        <p class="zh">所以蓝光（约 450 nm）被散射的强度大约是红光（约 700 nm）的 <strong>6–7 倍</strong>。这些被散射的蓝光被重新射向天空的各个方向，因此无论你看向哪里，都有来自四面八方的蓝光进入你的眼睛。</p>
        <p class="zh">两个很自然的问题：</p>
        <ul>
          <li class="zh"><strong>为什么不是紫色？</strong> 紫光其实比蓝光散射得还要强——但太阳发出的紫光更少，我们的眼睛对紫光也没那么敏感，而且有一部分紫光在上层大气中被吸收了。综合下来，平均的结果就是我们看到的蓝色。</li>
          <li class="zh"><strong>为什么日落是红色的？</strong> 日落时，阳光要穿过厚得多的大气。蓝光在到达你之前就已经被散射掉了，剩下长波长的红光和橙光直直地穿过来。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= LEVEL 3 ================= -->
  <section class="slide" id="l3">
    <div class="kicker">
      <span class="num">03</span>
      <span>Level Three · 第三层</span>
      <span class="rule"></span>
    </div>

    <div class="cols">
      <div class="col" lang="en">
        <h3><span class="chip">EN</span>For a Physics PhD 🔬</h3>
        <p>The blue sky is a direct macroscopic consequence of <strong>elastic (Rayleigh) scattering</strong> of solar radiation by subwavelength density fluctuations in the atmosphere.</p>
        <p><strong>The mechanism.</strong> Air is not a uniform medium; thermal motion creates fluctuating number densities of N₂ and O₂. Each fluctuation induces a dipole moment <span class="m">p</span> = <span class="m">α</span><span class="m">E</span> with molecular polarizability <span class="m">α</span>. The induced dipole radiates as a Hertzian oscillator, with a scattered power cross-section</p>
        <div class="eq">
          <span class="m">σ</span><sub>scatt</sub> =
          <span class="frac"><span>8<span class="m">π</span></span><span>3</span></span>
          <span style="font-style:normal">(</span><span class="frac"><span><span class="m">α</span></span><span>4<span class="m">π</span><span class="m">ε</span><sub>0</sub></span></span><span style="font-style:normal">)</span><sup>2</sup>
          <span class="frac"><span><span class="m">ω</span><sup>4</sup></span><span><span class="m">c</span><sup>4</sup></span></span>
          &nbsp;∝&nbsp;
          <span class="frac"><span>1</span><span><span class="m">λ</span><sup>4</sup></span></span>
        </div>
        <p>Because the scattering particle (molecule, ~0.3&nbsp;nm) is far smaller than <span class="m">λ</span> (~400–700&nbsp;nm), the quasistatic dipole approximation holds and radiation is emitted into the full 4<span class="m">π</span> steradians with a sin²<span class="m">θ</span> angular dependence (the dipole pattern) — though after integrating over the unpolarized incident sunlight and multiple scattering, the sky's skylight is partially linearly polarized, maximal at 90° from the Sun (the basis of the Haidinger brush and atmospheric polarization navigation).</p>
        <p><strong>Why the peak isn't in the violet.</strong> The spectral radiance reaching the observer is the product of the solar spectral irradiance, the <span class="m">λ</span><sup>−4</sup> scattering kernel, the transmission through the atmospheric column, and the observer's photopic luminosity function <span class="m">ȳ</span>(<span class="m">λ</span>). The solar spectrum peaks near 500&nbsp;nm and falls toward the UV; ozone absorption cuts off below ~320&nbsp;nm; and <span class="m">ȳ</span>(<span class="m">λ</span>) peaks at 555&nbsp;nm and drops sharply toward 400&nbsp;nm. Integrating these factors pushes the perceived chromaticity into the blue (~470–480&nbsp;nm peak of the scattered spectrum), not the violet.</p>
        <p><strong>The colorimetric statement.</strong> Under a clear sky the skylight's chromaticity coordinates (CIE 1931) sit near <span class="m">x</span> ≈ 0.24, <span class="m">y</span> ≈ 0.29 — markedly blue relative to the solar illuminant.</p>
        <p><strong>The red sunset, symmetrically.</strong> As the solar zenith angle grows, the optical air mass <span class="m">m</span>(<span class="m">θ</span>) ≈ 1/cos&nbsp;<span class="m">θ</span> (with refraction corrections near the horizon) increases the path length by an order of magnitude. The transmitted direct beam is attenuated by <span class="m">e</span><sup>−<span class="m">τ</span>(<span class="m">λ</span>)<span class="m">m</span></sup>, and since <span class="m">τ</span><sub>Rayleigh</sub> ∝ <span class="m">λ</span><sup>−4</sup>, the blue is depleted exponentially faster than the red — leaving the direct solar beam reddened and the anti-solar sky a deeper blue. Aerosol Mie scattering (∝ <span class="m">λ</span><sup>−1</sup> to <span class="m">λ</span><sup>0</sup>, forward-peaked) modulates this, which is why hazy skies look washed-out white rather than blue.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="col" lang="zh-Hans">
        <h3><span class="chip">中文</span>讲给物理学博士 🔬</h3>
        <p class="zh">蓝天是太阳辐射被大气中<strong>亚波长尺度的密度涨落</strong>发生的<strong>弹性（瑞利）散射</strong>的直接宏观结果。</p>
        <p class="zh"><strong>机制。</strong>空气不是均匀介质；热运动使 N₂ 和 O₂ 的数密度发生涨落。每个涨落都会诱导出一个偶极矩 <span class="m">p</span> = <span class="m">α</span><span class="m">E</span>，其中 <span class="m">α</span> 是分子极化率。这个诱导偶极子像赫兹振子一样辐射，其散射截面为</p>
        <div class="eq">
          <span class="m">σ</span><sub>scatt</sub> =
          <span class="frac"><span>8<span class="m">π</span></span><span>3</span></span>
          <span style="font-style:normal">(</span><span class="frac"><span><span class="m">α</span></span><span>4<span class="m">π</span><span class="m">ε</span><sub>0</sub></span></span><span style="font-style:normal">)</span><sup>2</sup>
          <span class="frac"><span><span class="m">ω</span><sup>4</sup></span><span><span class="m">c</span><sup>4</sup></span></span>
          &nbsp;∝&nbsp;
          <span class="frac"><span>1</span><span><span class="m">λ</span><sup>4</sup></span></span>
        </div>
        <p class="zh">由于散射粒子（分子，约 0.3 nm）远小于 <span class="m">λ</span>（约 400–700 nm），准静态偶极近似成立，辐射被发射到整个 4<span class="m">π</span> 立体角内，角分布为 sin²<span class="m">θ</span>（偶极图样）——不过，在对非偏振入射阳光和多次散射进行积分之后，天空光会表现出部分线偏振，且在距离太阳 90° 处达到最大（这正是海丁格刷现象和大气偏振导航的基础）。</p>
        <p class="zh"><strong>为什么峰值不在紫光。</strong>到达观察者的光谱辐亮度，是以下各项的乘积：太阳光谱辐照度、<span class="m">λ</span><sup>−4</sup> 散射核、穿过整层大气柱的透过率，以及观察者的明视觉光视效率函数 <span class="m">ȳ</span>(<span class="m">λ</span>)。太阳光谱在 500 nm 附近达到峰值，并向紫外方向下降；臭氧吸收在约 320 nm 以下形成截止；而 <span class="m">ȳ</span>(<span class="m">λ</span>) 在 555 nm 处达到峰值，并向 400 nm 方向急剧下降。把这些因子积分起来，就会把感知到的色度推向蓝色（散射光谱的峰值约在 470–480 nm），而不是紫色。</p>
        <p class="zh"><strong>色度学表述。</strong>在晴朗天空下，天空光的色度坐标（CIE 1931）大约位于 <span class="m">x</span> ≈ 0.24、<span class="m">y</span> ≈ 0.29——相对于太阳照明体而言明显偏蓝。</p>
        <p class="zh"><strong>对称地看红色日落。</strong>随着太阳天顶角增大，光学大气质量 <span class="m">m</span>(<span class="m">θ</span>) ≈ 1/cos&nbsp;<span class="m">θ</span>（在地平线附近还需考虑折射修正）会把路径长度增加一个数量级。透射的直射光束按 <span class="m">e</span><sup>−<span class="m">τ</span>(<span class="m">λ</span>)<span class="m">m</span></sup> 衰减，而由于 <span class="m">τ</span><sub>Rayleigh</sub> ∝ <span class="m">λ</span><sup>−4</sup>，蓝光比红光以指数级更快的速度被耗尽——于是直射太阳光束变红，而背着太阳一侧的天空则呈现更深的蓝色。气溶胶的米氏散射（∝ <span class="m">λ</span><sup>−1</sup> 到 <span class="m">λ</span><sup>0</sup>，且强烈前向）会调节这一过程，这就是为什么雾霾天看起来是发白的，而不是蓝色的。</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= CLOSING ================= -->
  <section class="closing" id="end">
    <div class="rule"></div>
    <p>In one sentence: short wavelengths scatter far more strongly off air molecules than long ones, so the sky fills with redirected blue light — and the same physics, read in reverse, paints the sunset red.</p>
    <p class="zh">一句话总结：短波长被空气分子散射的强度远大于长波长，于是天空充满了被重新定向的蓝光——而同样的物理，反过来看，就把日落染成了红色。</p>
    <footer>
      <span>Why Is the Sky Blue? · 天空为什么是蓝色的？</span>
      <span>Bilingual single-page edition · 双语单页版</span>
    </footer>
  </section>

</div>

<script>
(function () {
  "use strict";

  /* ---- scroll progress ---- */
  var bar = document.getElementById("progress");
  function onScroll() {
    var h = document.documentElement;
    var max = h.scrollHeight - h.clientHeight;
    bar.style.width = (max > 0 ? (h.scrollTop / max) * 100 : 0) + "%";
  }
  window.addEventListener("scroll", onScroll, { passive: true });
  window.addEventListener("resize", onScroll);
  onScroll();

